      "text": "To solve the problem \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\), we need to express each repeating decimal as a fraction.\n\nFirst, let's consider \\(0.\\overline{789}\\):\n\nLet \\(x = 0.\\overline{789}\\). Then,\n\\[ 1000x = 789.\\overline{789} \\]\nSubtracting the first equation from the second, we get:\n\\[ 1000x - x = 789.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{789} \\]\n\\[ 999x = 789 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{789}{999} \\]\n\nNext, let's consider \\(0.\\overline{456}\\):\n\nLet \\(y = 0.\\overline{456}\\). Then,\n\\[ 1000y = 456.\\overline{456} \\]\nSubtracting the first equation from the second, we get:\n\\[ 1000y - y = 456.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{456} \\]\n\\[ 999y = 456 \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{456}{999} \\]\n\nFinally, let's consider \\(0.\\overline{123}\\):\n\nLet \\(z = 0.\\overline{123}\\). Then,\n\\[ 1000z = 123.\\overline{123} \\]\nSubtracting the first equation from the second, we get:\n\\[ 1000z - z = 123.\\overline{123} - 0.\\overline{123} \\]\n\\[ 999z = 123 \\]\n\\[ z = \\frac{123}{999} \\]\n\nNow we need to find the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{789}{999} - \\frac{456}{999} - \\frac{123}{999} \\]\n\nSince the denominators are the same, we can combine the numerators:\n\\[ \\frac{789 - 456 - 123}{999} = \\frac{789 - 456 - 123}{999} = \\frac{210}{999} \\]\n\nSimplify the fraction \\(\\frac{210}{999}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{210}{999} = \\frac{210 \\div 3}{999 \\div 3} = \\frac{70}{333} \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\) is \\(\\frac{70}{333}\\). \n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\frac{70}{333}}\\)",
