      "text": "Let $x = 0.\\overline{789}$, and $y = 0.\\overline{456}$. Then we have $1000x = 789.\\overline{789}$, $100y = 456.\\overline{456}$, and $10y = 123.\\overline{123}$.\n\nWe subtract the second equation from the first: $1000x - 100y = 789.\\overline{789} - 456.\\overline{456} = 333.\\overline{333}$.\n\nThen we subtract the third equation from the first: $1000x - 10y = 789.\\overline{789} - 123.\\overline{123} = 666.\\overline{666}$.\n\nSo, $x - y - 10x = 333.\\overline{333}$, $9x = 333.\\overline{333}$, and $x = \\frac{111}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{37}{1}}$.\n\nCool, thanks for sharing...:) By the way if you have a math question, please post it in the homework tab (make sure your teacher it ok to post them however)\nGreat thing to know if you want to do math on your own, or if you forget any formulas :D\n\nAbsolutely true Omnomnomnom. You probably need to know the following.\n$11111111111111111111111111111=x$, the Try4Fun said.\n\n\"If no hardcore fundamental, straight number theory just pleas go out and post a question .....\" -bfaw\n\nThank you!  :) (I know your responses are helpful and I'll make sure to remember to post math questions on the highschool math forum.)",
