      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to convert each repeating decimal into a fraction. Each repeating decimal can be converted into a fraction by expressing it as an infinite series. We start with $0.\\overline{789}$.\n\nLet\n\\[ x = 0.\\overline{789}. \\]\nMultiplying $x$ by $1000$,\n\\[ 1000x = 789.\\overline{789}. \\]\nSubtracting the original $x$,\n\\[ 1000x - x = 789.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{789}, \\]\nwe find\n\\[ 999x = 789. \\]\nThus,\n\\[ x = \\frac{789}{999}. \\]\n\nSimilarly, convert and simplify $0.\\overline{456}$:\nLet\n\\[ y = 0.\\overline{456}. \\]\nMultiplying $y$ by $1000$,\n\\[ 1000y = 456.\\overline{456}. \\]\nSubtracting the original $y$,\n\\[ 1000y - y = 456.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{456}, \\]\nwe find\n\\[ 999y = 456. \\]\nThus,\n\\[ y = \\frac{456}{999}. \\]\n\nFinally, convert and simplify $0.\\overline{123}$:\nLet\n\\[ z = 0.\\overline{123}. \\]\nMultiplying $z$ by $1000$,\n\\[ 1000z = 123.\\overline{123}. \\]\nSubtracting the original $z$,\n\\[ 1000z - z = 123.\\overline{123} - 0.\\overline{123}, \\]\nwe find\n\\[ 999z = 123. \\]\nThus,\n\\[ z = \\frac{123}{999}. \\]\n\nGiven the values from the conversion, the expression\n\\[ 0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123} \\]\nbecomes\n\\[ \\frac{789}{999} - \\frac{456}{999} - \\frac{123}{999}. \\]\nSimplifying the fractions,\n\\[ \\frac{789 - 456 - 123}{999} = \\frac{210}{999}. \\]\n\nAs previous, this fraction needs to be simplified to its lowest terms:\n\\[ \\frac{210}{999} \\div \\frac{210}{210}, \\]\nwhich results in\n\\[ \\frac{210}{999} \\times \\frac{210}{210} = \\frac{44100}{210000} = \\frac{4410}{21000}. \\]\n\nContinue the process to simplify this final fraction to its lowest terms,\nFinally, the resulting simplified fraction is\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{21}{100}}. \\]",
