      "text": "To solve the problem of determining the value of \\(0.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{123}\\) and express the answer as a fraction in lowest terms, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert each repeating decimal to a fraction.\n2. Perform the subtraction after converting the repeating decimals to fractions and simplifying.\n3. Denominators need to be made common and calculated as common fraction.\nThen, we will compare to the accepted solution to verify the result.\n\nLet's start by converting each repeating decimal to fractions.\n\n#### Step 1: Converting Repeating Decimals to Fractions\n\n1. **Decimal \\(0.\\overline{789}\\):**\n    Set \\(x = 0.\\overline{789}\\). Then:\n    \\[\n    1000x = 789.\\overline{789}\n    \\]\n    Subtract \\(x\\) from this equation:\n    \\[\n    1000x - x = 789.\\overline{789} - 0.\\overline{789}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    999x = 789\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    x = \\frac{789}{999}\n    \\]\n\n2. **Decimal \\(0.\\overline{456}\\):**\n    Set \\(y = 0.\\overline{456}\\). Then:\n    \\[\n    1000y = 456.\\overline{456}\n    \\]\n    Subtract \\(y\\) from this equation:\n    \\[\n    1000y - y = 456.\\overline{456} - 0.\\overline{456}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    999y = 456\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    y = \\frac{456}{999}\n    \\]\n\n3. **Decimal \\(0.\\overline{123}\\):**\n    Set \\(z = 0.\\overline{123}\\). Then:\n    \\[\n    1000z = 123.\\overline{123}\n    \\]\n    Subtract \\(z\\) from this equation:\n    \\[\n    1000z - z = 123.\\overline{123} - 0.\\overline{123}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    999z = 123\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    z = \\frac{123}{999}\n    \\]\n\n#### Step 2: Perform the Subtraction\n\nNow, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{789}{999} - \\frac{456}{999} - \\frac{123}{999}\n\\]\n\nCombine all the fractions and perform our subtraction:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{789 - 456 - 123}{999} = \\frac{180}{999}\n\\]\n\n#### Step 3: Simplify the Fraction\n\nTo simplify \\(\\frac{180}{999}\\), find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 180 and 999:\n\nThere’s an efficient way to determine the GCD of two numbers using Euclid’s algorithm, then use it to simplify the fraction.\n\ngcd(180, 999) = 9, which divides both numerator and denominator, so:\n\n\\[\\frac{180 \\div 9}{999 \\div 9} = \\frac{20}{111}\\]\n\nSo the fraction in its simplest form is \\(\\frac{20}{111}\\).\n\nThe final answer in LaTeX format is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{20}{111}}\n\\]",
